<title>AUSTRIA: First Austrian, Giro detail H1.</title>
<headline>First Austrian, Giro detail H1.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>(in millions of schillings unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>							1997	1996</p>
<p>FIRST AUSTRIAN</p>
<p> Parent operating result			 855	 848</p>
<p> Parent operating income		     3,225     3,216</p>
<p> Parent net interest income		  1,956     1,967</p>
<p> Parent commission income			880	 792</p>
<p> Parent trading income			   207	 262</p>
<p> Parent operating expenses		   2,370     2,368</p>
<p> Parent personnel expenses		   1,530     1,554</p>
<p> Balance sheet total (versus end 1996) 235,112   224,567</p>
<p>GIROCREDIT</p>
<p> Parent operating				  722	 707</p>
<p> Parent operating income		     2,241     2,265</p>
<p> Parent net interest income		  1,600     1,708</p>
<p> Parent commission income			288	 319</p>
<p> Parent trading income			   341	 226</p>
<p> Parent operating expenses		   1,519     1,558</p>
<p> Personnel expenses				801	 769</p>
<p> Balance sheet total (versus end 1996) 379,799   339,724</p>
<p>NOTE - Die Erste Oesterreichische SparCasse-Bank (First Austrian) and GiroCredit are in the process of merging to form Austria's second largest banking group. First Austrian will account for 59 percent of the valuation of the new bank and GiroCredit for 41 percent. -- Vienna newsroom, +43-1 531 12 254</p>
